WEBVTT

00:00:00.200 --> 00:00:06.680
The OWASP Top 10 provides a practical recap of application risks: broken access control,

00:00:06.900 --> 00:00:11.780
cryptographic failures, injection, insecure design, misconfiguration,

00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:17.440
vulnerable components, authentication failures, integrity failures, logging failures,

00:00:17.660 --> 00:00:19.660
and SSRF.

00:00:19.880 --> 00:00:24.840
SOC 2 Trust Services Criteria help translate those risks into control expectations around

00:00:25.060 --> 00:00:26.580
logical access,

00:00:26.800 --> 00:00:33.120
system operations, monitoring, risk mitigation, change management, and data protection.

00:00:33.340 --> 00:00:38.780
Application security in cloud and SaaS environments is inseparable from customer trust.

00:00:39.000 --> 00:00:43.880
Customers expect secure design, reliable access controls, monitored operations,

00:00:44.100 --> 00:00:48.900
and disciplined change management. Completion of this course is awareness-level only.

00:00:49.120 --> 00:00:52.880
It does not constitute SOC 2 certification, audit completion,

00:00:53.100 --> 00:00:55.500
or proof of full organizational compliance.

00:00:55.720 --> 00:01:01.080
Useful follow-on materials include OWASP references, SOC 2 TSC references,

00:01:01.300 --> 00:01:06.340
secure coding checklists, a glossary, an OWASP-to-SOC 2 mapping matrix,

00:01:06.560 --> 00:01:10.400
developer quick-reference guides, and SaaS security checklists.

00:01:10.620 --> 00:01:13.500
Use this course as an awareness and planning aid.

00:01:13.720 --> 00:01:17.320
Validate criteria applicability with audit and compliance stakeholders.

00:01:17.540 --> 00:01:23.540
Maintain evidence for secure development, monitoring, access control, change management,

00:01:23.760 --> 00:01:25.680
and remediation activities.

00:01:25.900 --> 00:01:32.460
Selected SOC 2 mappings for this topic include CC6.1 - Logical access controls;

00:01:32.680 --> 00:01:39.400
CC7.1 - Vulnerability management; CC8.1 - Change management processes.
